{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391870-doubts-about-an-effect","id":1391870,"title":"Doubts about an effect","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-26T23:26:49-07:00","id":1391870,"title":"Doubts about an effect","content":"Last session one of my players used Correspondence 2 and Life 2 to &quot;adapt&quot; to an enemy's movements, so it was easier for her to face the bad guy in combat. I let her use that, with many doubts (not an important bad guy anyways), but the combination didnt sound completely right in my head. <br /> <br /> According to the M20 ruleset, what do you need to do a similar effect?<br /> <br /> (Thinking about it, with Corr 2 Life 2 she couldve set a minor ward against that particular target..)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","user":"Argonot","date":". 05-27-2020, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T00:32:20-07:00","id":1391879,"title":"","content":"There are many ways to improvice your chances in combat, but...Corr 2 Life 2 certainly seems strange there, if anything for the Life component.<br /> <br /> Usually, improving your chance for high initiative, or to hit and/or dodge involve things like<br /> <br /> Time 1 - Perfect timing<br /> Time 2 - Sensing ahead 1-3 seconds<br /> Time 3 - additional actions, celerity style<br /> Entropy 1 - sense weak spots<br /> Entropy 2 - Increase the odds<br /> Life 1 - Also sense weak spots, in organics<br /> Matter 1 - sense weak spots in synthetics<br /> Forces 2 - Subtly redirect forces<br /> Mind 1 - Mental multitasking - you can think about a mathematical formula while in the midst of combat. Theoretically simply allows the ability to do a mental roll as well as a physical roll in the same round. Potentially a good idea if you want to do something physical as well as roll Arete.<br /> Mind 2 - Sense the surface thoughts/impulses of the enemy a moment ahead<br /> Correspondence 1 - Perfectly sense distances<br /> Correspondence 2 - Appear subtly shifted into a direction just a bit<br /> Correspondence 2 - Can be used to give yourself a sort of 360 degree sense, which is neat for avoiding blind spots.<br /> <br /> Life can be used in the way that you can raise your physical stats with Life 3, really. That's the kind of adaptation that sphere can do. It can also allow soaking lethal/Aggravated.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And yes, it also shows that people should not underestimate Mages with level 1 spheres in plain, physical fisticuffs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-27-2020, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T05:19:57-07:00","id":1391899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391870-doubts-about-an-effect#post1391870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the M20 ruleset, what do you need to do a similar effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not aware in M20 of a rote to to &quot;adapt to an enemy's movements &quot;.<br /> <br /> A similar rote I once casted: Correspondence 1/Time 1 to sense the &quot;rithm&quot; of an enemy (to perfectly time the movements - speed it's a relation between space and time). Considering how important this is for real life combat (as per the book of five rings - not a Mage book, but recomended for Akashics), that should accrue a bonus<br /> <br /> I think Life 2/Corr 2 could work too, albeit I would say Corr 1 should be enough for your magick to react to enemy space . Then you want to make your body automatically react to the data?, that should be well within the subtle domain of your own body Life 2 grants (Life 2 allows fine control your own breath, metabolism, pulse, and other subtle aspects of your Life pattern, doesn't it?).<br /> You're magick guide your body, bypassing the need to consciously react - improving reaction time. It could lead to some comic relief if the character under such a spell needs to either be very specific about the target/s, or make a check to *avoid* hitting anyone that comes dangerously close. God knows that MA reflexes can play such a trick - and if you let your magick react for ya, well, you're asking for it :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-27-2020, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T05:32:16-07:00","id":1391901,"title":"","content":"I'd allow that with Correspondence 1/Life 2. All you're doing is scanning the enemy's movements with Correspondence and then improving your capabilities with Life. It's a nice little rote. You can do the same with other Spheres too (Entropy 1 and Time 1 spring to mind). You can use the rules for magick affecting abilities, and give a difficulty break of one point per success, to a maximum of three to keep the Effect within reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T09:50:25-07:00","id":1391977,"title":"","content":"Seems more like the typical Correspondence 2 Forces 2 of blurring space and movement so you react better to the foe's actions.<br /> <br /> That being said, since Correspondence 2 and Life 2 is minor warding and spatial mutations and Life 2 is cosmetic adaptions and being able to better control adrenaline (so not be so jumpy), it would be ok if there was a good Focus-based explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T09:58:50-07:00","id":1391979,"title":"","content":"I'm with Aleph and Thebian, they'd just need Correspondence 1 and Life 2. Probably the same die difficulty depending on foci.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}